🚽 Test case: #193 -- returning a struct-returning call result whose type
🚽 does not match the declared return type (`bussin mk();` where `mk`
🚽 returns `gang Other` but the function returns `gang Point`) is rejected
🚽 at the return statement, and the temporary return blob is freed (no leak).
gang Point {
    rizz x;
};
gang Other {
    rizz z;
};

gang Other mk() {
    gang Other o;
    o.z = 1;
    bussin o;
}

gang Point relay() {
    bussin mk();
}

skibidi main {
    gang Point p = relay();
    bussin 0;
}
